<title>
Variable Displacement Oil Pump Description
</title>
<ptxt>
The variable displacement oil pump assembly mainly consists of an inner rotor (1), vanes (2), cam ring (3), cam ring spring (4) and variable oil pump valve (5). Sucked oil (6) by rotating vanes is compressed and discharged (7) toward oil filter. The cam ring is supported by the cam ring spring on a pivot pin (8) and changes the position to advance (cam spring expanded position for high discharge) or retard (cam spring compressed by oil pressure (9) through the variable oil pump valve for low discharge) and the discharged oil volume and pressure is controlled by ECM monitoring condition of the engine. Through this discharge control, oil is supplied optimally avoiding useless engine load for the pumping action.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Further, the oil management has eliminated conventional oil relief valve from the pump.
</ptxt>
